  "question": {
    "text": "If $S_n=\\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{1}{{ }^n C_r}$ and $t_n=\\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{r}{{ }^n C_r}$, then $\\frac{t_n}{S_n}$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "g6DUr",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{n}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xZwf9",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} n-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0GHzh",
      "text": "\n$n-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "csBkE",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 n-1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$t=\\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{r}{{ }^n C_r}=\\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{n-r}{{ }^n C_{n-r}}=\\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{n-r}{{ }^n C_r}\\left(\\because{ }^n C_r={ }^n C_{n-r}\\right)$\n$2 t_n=\\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{r+n-r}{{ }^n C_r}=\\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{n}{{ }^n C_r} \\Rightarrow t_n=\\frac{n}{2} \\sum_{r=0}^n \\frac{1}{{ }^n C_r}=\\frac{n}{2} S_n \\Rightarrow \\frac{t_n}{S_n}=\\frac{n}{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
